<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maurya Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mauryas, Mauryan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Maurya Empire was the first state to unite most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandragupta-maurya">Chandragupta Maurya</a> around 321 BCE. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a> it reached its greatest extent, and Ashoka's edicts promoted dhamma and Buddhist ethics. It had a centralised administration described in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthashastra">Arthashastra</a> and declined after Ashoka's death, ending around 185 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maurya-empire.jpg" alt="Maurya Empire" width="320" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joshua Jonathan · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maurya_Empire,_c.250_BCE_network_model_v01.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
